% decline_reader_bad.glp — FR-036 DECLINE (NEGATIVE: must be REJECTED at load).
% reader/1 is NON-MONOTONIC: it succeeds on an unbound reader, then a later bind
% makes it false — so a committed verdict can be falsified, which is unsound
% across a link (a withheld/late remote bind makes the committed guard wrong).
% It violates the FR-039 monotone-commit invariant and is never introduced. This
% file is identical in shape to atom_guard.glp's is_atom except the declined
% guard, so the rejection (undefined guard predicate) isolates the decline.
exported procedure dreader(_?, _).
dreader(X, yes) :- reader(X?) | true.
